{"id": "unknown-2026-10-29-009", "date": "2026-10-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Swiss textile machinery firms gear up for China and India trade shows", "content": "China and India present distinct opportunities for Swiss textile machinery suppliers. \nChina prioritises automation, digital connectivity and resource efficiency, while India focuses on modernisation, capacity expansion and quality control. \nAround 20 Swiss Textile Machinery member companies will exhibit at ITMA Asia + CITME in Shanghai in November and India ITME in Greater Noida in December 2026.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/swiss-textile-machinery-firms-gear-up-for-china-and-india-trade-shows-314642-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-29-010", "date": "2026-10-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "CITI says revamped textile PLI scheme will boost investment in India", "content": "India’s textile PLI portal will reopen for new Round 4 applications from November 1 to December 31, 2026, CITI said, welcoming the Union Ministry of Textiles’ move.\nCITI said a lower turnover threshold and longer-term horizon would widen participation and support investment.\nThe round would aid MMF apparel, MMF fabrics and technical textiles; sector exports rose 17.51 per cent in September.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/citi-says-revamped-textile-pli-scheme-will-boost-investment-in-india-314641-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-29-011", "date": "2026-10-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["improve", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "North India’s cotton yarn market bearish, Ludhiana prices fall", "content": "North India's cotton yarn markets remained bearish as Ludhiana prices fell, while Delhi held steady amid weak demand and payment constraints.\nPanipat recycled yarn demand improved slightly, but prices were unchanged; recycled polyester fibre rose on PET bottle shortages.\nCotton stayed stable despite lower kapas and binola rates, with arrivals at 14,600 bales.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/north-india-s-cotton-yarn-market-bearish-ludhiana-prices-fall-314643-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-29-012", "date": "2026-10-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India ITME Society announces winners of 2026 ITME Technical Awards", "content": "India ITME Society announced its fourth Technical Awards winners, recognising Luwa India, Lakshmi Card Clothing, Deven Supercriticals, Artitech Innovations and four young researchers.\nLate Dr D. Jayavarthanavelu will be honoured as a Titan of Textile Engineering.\nThe awards ceremony on December 6 in Greater Noida will follow a CEO Conclave focused on technology-led competitiveness.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-itme-society-announces-winners-of-2026-itme-technical-awards-314619-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-29-013", "date": "2026-10-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India approves $1.05 bn container manufacturing scheme", "content": "India’s Cabinet has approved a Rs 10,000 crore (~$1.05 billion) Container Manufacturing Promotion Scheme up to FY 2039-40 to expand domestic container capacity and cut import dependence. \nIt provides interest subvention, operational expenditure support, and testing and certification assistance. \nTargets include capacity of up to 7.5 lakh TEUs, 3,000 direct jobs and over 50,000 indirect jobs. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-approves-1-05-bn-container-manufacturing-scheme-314626-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
